  "text": "In November 2014 we spoke, for the most part, as one instrument pointed at a single object. On 2014-11-14, 68 of us said \"the keystone xl pipeline,\" the day our alignment peaked. That day 41 of us said \"approve the keystone,\" 39 said \"approve the keystone xl,\" and 38 said \"approve the keystone xl pipeline.\" John Hoeven first said \"the keystone xl pipeline\" on 2013-01-22, and we were still saying it nearly two years later. The variants converged on one act: 38 of us said \"to approve the keystone,\" 38 said \"of the keystone xl,\" 37 said \"of the keystone xl pipeline,\" 37 said \"to approve the keystone xl.\" Every one of these peaked on the same day, 2014-11-14. We record that our most-repeated words that month named one pipeline, and that we named it together.",
